            element_info: Some((
                atomic_number: 8,
                atomic_weight: 15.999,
                group: Some(16),
                period: Some(2),
                block: Some("p"),
                electron_config: Some("[He] 2s2 2p4"),
                electronegativity_pauling: Some(3.44),
                first_ionization_kj_mol: Some(1313.938036675),
                electron_affinity_kj_mol: Some(140.9755360475),
                atomic_radius_pm: Some(60.0),
                discoverer: Some("Joseph Priestly, Carl Wilhelm Scheele"),
                discovery_year: Some(1774),
                overview: Some("Oxygen is a chemical element; it has the symbol O and its atomic number is 8. It is a member of the chalcogen group in the periodic table, a highly reactive nonmetal, and a potent oxidizing agent that readily forms oxides with most elements as well as with other compounds. Oxygen is the most abundant element in Earth's crust, making up almost half of the Earth's crust in the form of various oxides such as water, carbon dioxide, iron oxides and silicates. It is also the third-most abundant element in the universe after hydrogen and helium.

At standard temperature and pressure, two oxygen atoms will bind covalently to form dioxygen, a colorless and odorless diatomic gas with the chemical formula O2. Dioxygen gas currently constitutes approximately 20.95% molar fraction of the Earth's atmosphere, though this has changed considerably over long periods of time in Earth's history. A much rarer triatomic allotrope of oxygen, ozone (O3), strongly absorbs the UVB and UVC wavelengths and forms a protective ozone layer at the lower stratosphere, which shields the biosphere from ionizing ultraviolet radiation. However, ozone present at the surface is a corrosive byproduct of smog and thus an air pollutant."),
                discovery_story: None,
                isotopes_summary: Some("18 known isotopes; stable: 16O (99.8%), 18O (20.4%), 17O (3.8%), 27O; 13 radioactive"),
                magnetic_ordering: None,
            )),
        ),
