            decay_product_id: None,
            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [],
            description: Some("Anisole, or methoxybenzene, is an organic compound with the formula CH3OC6H5.  It is a colorless liquid with a smell reminiscent of anise seed, and in fact many of its derivatives are found in natural and artificial fragrances. The compound is mainly made synthetically and is a precursor to other synthetic compounds. Structurally, it is an ether (−O−) with a methyl (−CH3) and phenyl (−C6H5) group attached.  Anisole is a standard reagent of both practical and pedagogical value."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H226 (> 99.9%): Flammable liquid and vapor [Warning Flammable liquids]"),
            uses: ["Computer and Electronic Product Manufacturing", "IN PERFUMERY; IN ORGANIC SYNTHESES", "Solvent", "VERMICIDE; FLAVORING"],
            logp: Some(1.695),
            appearance: Some("Anisole appears as a clear straw-colored liquid with an aromatic odor. Insoluble in water and the same density as water. Vapors heavier than air. Moderately toxic by ingestion. A skin irritant. Used to make perfumes, flavorings and as a solvent."),
            synonyms: ["Anisol", "Methoxybenzene", "phenoxymethane", "Methyl phenyl ether", "Phenol methyl ether", "phenyl methyl ether", "100-66-3", "Benzene, methoxy-"],
            references: [("Wikipedia", "https://en.wikipedia.org/?curid=1481286"), ("PubChem", "https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/7519"), ("ChEBI", "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI_16579"), ("Wikidata", "http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q312244"), ("NIST", "https://webbook.nist.gov/cgi/cbook.cgi?ID=C100663&Units=SI")],
