            description: Some("Barium nitrate is the inorganic compound of barium with the nitrate anion, having the chemical formula Ba(NO3)2. It, like most barium salts, is colorless, toxic, and water-soluble. It burns with a green flame and is an oxidizer; the compound is commonly used in pyrotechnics."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H272 (68.7%): May intensify fire; oxidizer [Danger Oxidizing liquids; Oxidizing solids]"),
            uses: ["Oxidizing/reducing agents", "All Other Basic Inorganic Chemical Manufacturing"],
            logp: Some(-0.729),
            appearance: Some("Barium nitrate appears as a white crystalline solid. Noncombustible, but accelerates burning of combustible materials. If large quantities are involved in fire or the combustible material is finely divided, an explosion may result. May explode under prolonged exposure to heat or fire. Toxic oxides of nitrogen produced in fires."),
            synonyms: ["nitrobarite", "nitrato barico", "barium dinitrate", "nitrate de baryum", "barium(II) nitrate", "nitric acid barium salt", "barium(II) nitrate (1:2)", "nitric acid, barium salt"],
            references: [("Wikipedia", "https://en.wikipedia.org/?curid=1112725"), ("PubChem", "https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/156588334"), ("ChEBI", "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI_190440"), ("Wikidata", "http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q407666"), ("NIST", "https://webbook.nist.gov/cgi/cbook.cgi?ID=C10022318&Units=SI")],
            element_info: None,
