            standard_potential_v: None,
            half_life_seconds: None,
            decay_product_id: None,
            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [],
            description: Some("Nitrogen dioxide is a chemical compound with the formula NO2. One of several nitrogen oxides, nitrogen dioxide is a reddish-brown gas.  It is a paramagnetic, bent molecule with C2v point group symmetry. Industrially, NO2 is an intermediate in the synthesis of nitric acid, millions of tons of which are produced each year, primarily for the production of fertilizers. 
Nitrogen dioxide is poisonous and can be fatal if inhaled in large quantities. Cooking with a gas stove produces nitrogen dioxide which causes poorer indoor air quality. Combustion of gas can lead to increased concentrations of nitrogen dioxide throughout the home environment which is linked to respiratory issues and diseases. The LC50 (median lethal dose)  for humans has been estimated to be 174 ppm for a 1-hour exposure. It is also included in the NOx family of atmospheric pollutants."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H270: May cause or intensify fire; oxidizer [Danger Oxidizing gases]"),
            uses: [],
            logp: Some(0.098),
            appearance: Some("Nitrogen dioxide appears as a reddish brown gas or yellowish-brown liquid when cooled or compressed. Shipped as a liquefied gas under own vapor pressure. Vapors are heavier than air. Toxic by inhalation (vapor) and skin absorption. Noncombustible, but accelerates the burning of combustible materials. Cylinders and ton containers may not be equipped with a safety relief device."),
            synonyms: ["NO2", "[NO2]", "NO2(.)", "ONO(.)", "nitryl", "(NO2)(.)", "nitrosooxidanyl", "Stickstoffdioxid"],
            references: [("Wikipedia", "https://en.wikipedia.org/?curid=238528"), ("PubChem", "https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/3032552"), ("ChEBI", "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI_33101"), ("Wikidata", "http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q207895"), ("NIST", "https://webbook.nist.gov/cgi/cbook.cgi?ID=C10102440&Units=SI")],
            element_info: None,
