            standard_potential_v: None,
            half_life_seconds: None,
            decay_product_id: None,
            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [],
            description: Some("Calcium nitrate are inorganic compounds with the formula Ca(NO3)2·(H2O)x. The anhydrous compound, which is rarely encountered, absorbs moisture from the air to give the tetrahydrate. Both anhydrous and hydrated forms are colourless salts. Hydrated calcium nitrate, also called Norgessalpeter (Norwegian salpeter), is mainly used as a component in fertilizers, but it has other applications. Nitrocalcite is the name for a mineral which is a hydrated calcium nitrate that forms as an efflorescence where manure contacts concrete or limestone in a dry environment as in stables or caverns. A variety of related salts are known including calcium ammonium nitrate decahydrate and calcium potassium nitrate decahydrate."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H272 (26.9%): May intensify fire; oxidizer [Danger Oxidizing liquids; Oxidizing solids]"),
            uses: ["Agricultural chemicals (non-pesticidal)", "Chemical reaction regulator", "Drier", "Fuels and fuel additives", "Intermediates", "Odor agents"],
            logp: Some(-0.729),
            appearance: Some("Calcium nitrate appears as white to light gray granular solid. May be either the anhydrous compound or the tetrahydrate. Used in fertilizers, explosives and pyrotechnics."),
            synonyms: ["Saltpeter", "Lime nitrate", "Lime saltpeter", "Norge saltpeter", "Norway saltpeter", "Calcium saltpeter", "calcium dinitrate", "Norwegian saltpeter"],
            references: [("Wikipedia", "https://en.wikipedia.org/?curid=1737419"), ("PubChem", "https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/156589053"), ("ChEBI", "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI_64205"), ("Wikidata", "http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q407392"), ("NIST", "https://webbook.nist.gov/cgi/cbook.cgi?ID=C10124375&Units=SI")],
            element_info: None,
        ),
