            standard_potential_v: None,
            half_life_seconds: None,
            decay_product_id: None,
            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [],
            description: Some("Cinnamyl acetate (3-phenylprop-2-enyl acetate) is a chemical compound of the cinnamyl ester family, in which the variable R group is substituted by a methyl group. As a result of the non-aromatic carbon-carbon double bond, cinnamyl acetate can exist in a Z and an E configuration:

Cinnamyl acetate naturally occurs in fresh bark of cinnamon (Cinnamomum zeylanicum Blume and other Cinnamomum species), with concentrations of 2,800–51,000 ppm.
Cinnamyl acetate is used as a flavor ester in for example bread and animal feed and has a sweet floral-fruity fragrance.  Moreover, it is used in several cosmetics, some toiletries but also in non-cosmetic products such as detergents."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: None,
            uses: ["Fragrance", "CIR ingredient: Cinnamyl Acetate"],
