            uses: ["Other Solid"],
            logp: Some(-0.374),
            appearance: Some("Maleic anhydride appears as colorless crystalline needles, flakes, pellets, rods, briquettes, lumps or a fused mass. Melts at 113 °F. Shipped both as a solid and in the molten state. Vapors, fumes and dusts strong irritate the eyes, skin and mucous membranes. Flash point 218 °F. Autoignition temperature 890 °F. Used to make paints and plastics and other chemicals."),
