            properties: [IsAcid],
            description: Some("Butyl butyrate, or butyl butanoate, is an organic compound that is an ester formed by the condensation of butyric acid and n-butanol.  It is a clear, colorless liquid that is insoluble in water, but miscible with ethanol and diethyl ether. Its refractive index is 1.406 at 20 °C."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H226: Flammable liquid and vapor [Warning Flammable liquids]"),
            uses: ["Fragrance", "All Other Basic Organic Chemical Manufacturing", "Intermediate"],
            logp: Some(2.13),
            appearance: Some("Butyl butyrate appears as a colorless liquid. Insoluble in water. A marine pollutant. Poses a threat to the aquatic environment. Immediate steps should be taken to prevent spread to the environment. May penetrate soils and contaminate groundwater and nearby waterways. Mildly irritates the eyes and skin."),
            synonyms: ["butyl butanoate", "1-butyl butyrate", "butyl n-butyrate", "n-butyl butyrate", "n-butyl butanoate", "n-butyl n-butyrate", "sec-butyl butyrate", "n-butyl n-butanoate"],
