            properties: [],
            description: Some("Furan is a heterocyclic organic compound, consisting of a five-membered aromatic ring with four carbon atoms and one oxygen atom.  Chemical compounds containing such rings are also referred to as furans.
Furan is a colorless, flammable, highly volatile liquid with a boiling point close to room temperature. It is soluble in common organic solvents, including alcohol, ether, and acetone, and is slightly soluble in water.  Its odor is \"strong, ethereal; chloroform-like\".  It is toxic and may be carcinogenic in humans. Furan is used as a starting point for other speciality chemicals."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H224: Extremely flammable liquid and vapor [Danger Flammable liquids]"),
            uses: ["All Other Basic Organic Chemical Manufacturing", "CHEMICAL INTERMEDIATE FOR TETRAHYDROFURAN", "Intermediate", "Plastics Product Manufacturing"],
            logp: Some(1.28),
            appearance: Some("Furan appears as a clear colorless liquid with a strong odor. Flash point below 32 °F. Less dense than water and insoluble in water. Vapors heavier than air."),
