            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [IsMetal, IsBase],
            description: Some("Potassium hydroxide is an inorganic compound with the formula KOH, and is commonly called caustic potash.
Along with sodium hydroxide (NaOH), KOH is a prototypical strong base. It has many industrial and niche applications, most of which utilize its caustic nature and its reactivity toward acids. About 2.5 million tonnes were produced in 2023. KOH is noteworthy as the precursor to most soft and liquid soaps, as well as numerous potassium-containing chemicals.  It is a white solid that is dangerously corrosive."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H314: Causes severe skin burns and eye damage [Danger Skin corrosion/irritation]"),
            uses: ["Adsorbents and absorbents", "Agricultural chemicals (non-pesticidal)", "Anti-freeze agent", "Bleaching agents", "Catalyst", "Cleaning agent"],
            logp: Some(-0.938),
            appearance: Some("Potassium hydroxide, solution appears as an clear aqueous solution. Corrosive to metals and tissue. Noncombustible. Used in chemical manufacturing, petroleum refining, cleaning compounds."),
            synonyms: ["KOH", "lye", "E525", "Aetzkali", "potash lye", "Kaliumhydroxid", "caustic potash", "potasse caustique"],
