            standard_potential_v: None,
            half_life_seconds: None,
            decay_product_id: None,
            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [],
            description: Some("Benzyl acetate is an organic ester with the molecular formula CH3C(O)OCH2C6H5. It is formed by the condensation of benzyl alcohol and acetic acid.
Similar to most other esters, it possesses a sweet and pleasant aroma, owing to which, it finds applications in personal hygiene and health care products. It is a constituent of jasmin and of the essential oils of ylang-ylang and neroli. It has pleasant sweet aroma reminiscent of jasmine. Further as a flavoring agent it is also used to impart jasmine or apple flavors to various cosmetics and personal care products like lotions, hair creams etc..
It is one of many compounds that is attractive to males of various species of orchid bees. It is collected and used by the bees as an intra-specific pheromone; In apiculture benzyl acetate is used as a bait to collect bees. Natural sources of benzyl acetate include varieties of flowers like jasmine (Jasminum), and fruits like pear, apple, etc."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H370: Causes damage to organs [Danger Specific target organ toxicity, single exposure]"),
            uses: ["Fragrance", "Odor agents", "Processing aids not otherwise specified", "All Other Basic Organic Chemical Manufacturing"],
            logp: Some(1.75),
            appearance: Some("Benzyl acetate is a colorless liquid with an odor of pears. (USCG, 1999)"),
            synonyms: ["Benzyl ethanoate", "phenylmethyl acetate", "Phenylmethyl ethanoate", "Acetic acid, benzyl ester", "Acetic acid, phenylmethyl ester", "140-11-4", "Acetic acid benzyl ester", "alpha-Acetoxytoluene"],
            references: [("Wikipedia", "https://en.wikipedia.org/?curid=3218316"), ("PubChem", "https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/8785"), ("ChEBI", "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI_52051"), ("Wikidata", "http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q424223"), ("NIST", "https://webbook.nist.gov/cgi/cbook.cgi?ID=C140114&Units=SI")],
            element_info: None,
