            properties: [IsAcid],
            description: Some("Ricinoleic acid, formally called 12-hydroxy-9-cis-octadecenoic acid, is a fatty acid.  It is an unsaturated omega-9 fatty acid and a hydroxy acid. It is a major component of the seed oil obtained from the seeds of castor plant (Ricinus communis L., Euphorbiaceae), the plant that produces ricin. It is also found in the sclerotium of ergot (Claviceps purpurea Tul., Clavicipitaceae). About 90% of the fatty acid content in castor oil is the ricinolein."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H315 (33.3%): Causes skin irritation [Warning Skin corrosion/irritation]"),
