            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [IsMetal, IsAcid],
            description: Some("Potassium sorbate is the potassium salt of sorbic acid, structural formula CH3CH=CH−CH=CH−CO2K.  It is a white salt that is very soluble in water (58.2% at 20 °C).  It is primarily used as a food preservative (E number 202). Potassium sorbate is effective in a variety of applications including food, wine, and personal care products. While sorbic acid occurs naturally in rowan and hippophae berries, virtually all of the world's supply of sorbic acid, from which potassium sorbate is derived, is manufactured synthetically."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H319: Causes serious eye irritation [Warning Serious eye damage/eye irritation]"),
            uses: ["Preservative", "Processing aids, not otherwise listed", "Stabilizing agent", "Agriculture, Forestry, Fishing and Hunting", "All Other Basic Organic Chemical Manufacturing"],
            logp: Some(0.823),
            appearance: None,
            synonyms: ["Potassium (E,E)-sorbate", "sorbic acid potassium salt", "potassium trans,trans-sorbate", "Potassium (E,E)-2,4-hexadienoate", "2,4-hexadienoic acid potassium salt", "potassium (2E,4E)-hexa-2,4-dienoate", "potassium trans,trans-2,4-hexadienoate", "24634-61-5"],
            references: [("Wikipedia", "https://en.wikipedia.org/?curid=2904331"), ("PubChem", "https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/74219106"), ("ChEBI", "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI_77868"), ("Wikidata", "http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q410744"), ("NIST", "https://webbook.nist.gov/cgi/cbook.cgi?ID=C24634615&Units=SI")],
