            decay_product_id: None,
            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [IsMetal],
            description: Some("Sodium nitrite is an inorganic compound with the chemical formula NaNO2. It is a white to slightly yellowish crystalline powder that is very soluble in water and is hygroscopic. From an industrial perspective, it is the most important nitrite salt. It is a precursor to a variety of organic compounds, such as pharmaceuticals, dyes, and pesticides, but it is probably best known as a food additive used in processed meats and (in some countries) in fish products."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H272: May intensify fire; oxidizer [Danger Oxidizing liquids; Oxidizing solids]"),
            uses: ["Corrosion inhibitor", "Corrosion inhibitors and anti-scaling agents", "Oxidizing agent", "UV stabilizer", "Adhesion/cohesion promoter"],
            logp: Some(-0.239),
            appearance: Some("Sodium nitrite appears as a yellowish white crystalline solid. Noncombustible but will accelerate the burning of combustible material. If large quantities are involved in a fire or if the combustible material is finely divided, an explosion may result. If contaminated by ammonium compounds, spontaneous decomposition can occur and the resulting heat may ignite surrounding combustible material. Prolonged exposure heat may result in an explosion. Toxic oxides of nitrogen are produced in fires involving this material. Used as a food preservative, and to make other chemicals."),
            synonyms: ["E250", "NaNO2", "7632-00-0", "Natrium nitrit", "Nitrito sodico", "Nitrite de sodium", "nitrous acid, sodium salt", "Nitrite, sodium"],
            references: [("Wikipedia", "https://en.wikipedia.org/?curid=407615"), ("PubChem", "https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/24188564"), ("ChEBI", "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI_78870"), ("Wikidata", "http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q339975"), ("NIST", "https://webbook.nist.gov/cgi/cbook.cgi?ID=C7632000&Units=SI")],
            element_info: None,
