            properties: [],
            description: Some("Isoprene, or 2-methyl-1,3-butadiene, is a common volatile organic compound with the formula CH2=C(CH3)−CH=CH2. In its pure form it is a colorless volatile liquid. It is produced by many plants and animals (including humans) and its polymers are the main component of natural rubber."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H224: Extremely flammable liquid and vapor [Danger Flammable liquids]"),
            uses: ["Intermediates", "Monomers", "Processing aids, not otherwise listed", "Adhesive Manufacturing", "All Other Basic Organic Chemical Manufacturing"],
            logp: Some(1.748),
            appearance: Some("Isoprene, stabilized appears as a clear colorless liquid with a petroleum-like odor. Density 5.7 lb / gal. Flash point -65 °F. Boiling point 93 °F. May polymerize exothermically if heated or contaminated. If polymerization takes place inside a closed container, the container may rupture violently. Less dense than water and insoluble in water. Vapors heavier than air."),
            synonyms: ["Isopren", "isopreno", "isoterpene", "isopentadiene", "2-methyldivinyl", "CH2=C(CH3)CH=CH2", "2-methylbutadiene", "beta-methylbivinyl"],
