            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [IsAcid],
            description: Some("Propionic acid (, from the Greek words πρῶτος : prōtos, meaning \"first\", and πίων : píōn, meaning \"fat\"; also known as propanoic acid) is a naturally occurring carboxylic acid with chemical formula CH3CH2CO2H. It is an oily liquid with a pungent and unpleasant smell. The anion CH3CH2CO−2 as well as the salts and esters of propionic acid are known as propionates or propanoates.
About half of the world production of propionic acid is consumed as a preservative for both animal feed and food for human consumption. It is also useful as an intermediate in the production of other chemicals, especially polymers."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H314: Causes severe skin burns and eye damage [Danger Skin corrosion/irritation]"),
