            decay_particle_id: None,
            properties: [],
            description: Some("Picric acid is an organic compound with the formula (O2N)3C6H2OH. Its IUPAC name is 2,4,6-trinitrophenol (TNP). The name \"picric\" comes from Greek: πικρός (pikros), meaning \"bitter\", due to its bitter taste. It is one of the most acidic phenols. Like other strongly nitrated organic compounds, picric acid is an explosive, which is its primary use. It has also been used as medicine (antiseptic, burn treatments) and as a dye."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H201: (Deleted) Explosive; mass explosion hazard [Danger Explosives]"),
