            properties: [],
            description: Some("Guaiacol () is an organic compound with the formula C6H4(OH)(OCH3). It is a phenolic compound containing a methoxy functional group. Guaiacol appears as a viscous colorless oil, although aged or impure samples are often yellowish.  It occurs widely in nature and is a common product of the pyrolysis of wood."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H318: Causes serious eye damage [Danger Serious eye damage/eye irritation]"),
            uses: ["All Other Basic Organic Chemical Manufacturing", "Direct-acting or stimulant expectorant", "Intermediate"],
            logp: Some(1.401),
            appearance: Some("O-methoxyphenol appears as colorless to amber crystals or liquid. Density (of solid) 1.129 g / cm3. Solidifies at 28 °C (82.4 °F), but may remain liquid for a long time even at a much lower temperature. Slightly water soluble. Soluble in aqueous sodium hydroxide. Used medicinally as an expectorant. Used, because of its anti-oxidant properties, as an anti-skinning agent for paints."),
            synonyms: ["Guajol", "Guasol", "Anastil", "Creodon", "Guaicol", "Guiacol", "Guajakol", "Guaiastil"],
