            properties: [IsBase],
            description: Some("Quinaldine or 2-methylquinoline is an organic compound with the formula CH3C9H6N.  It is one of the methyl derivatives of the heterocyclic compound quinoline.  It is bioactive and is used in the preparation of various dyes.  It is a colorless oil but commercial samples can appear colored."),
            text_source: Some("Wikipedia"),
            hazard_summary: Some("H302+H312 (26.8%): Harmful if swallowed or in contact with skin [Warning Acute toxicity, oral; acute toxicity, dermal]"),
            uses: ["Surface active agents"],
            logp: Some(2.543),
            appearance: Some("Quinaldine appears as a colorless oily liquid darkening to red-brown on exposure to air. Flash point 175 °F. Denser than water and slightly soluble in water. Vapors heavier than air. Produces toxic oxides of nitrogen during combustion. Used to make dyes, pharmaceuticals and other chemicals."),
            synonyms: ["quinaldine", "2-methyl-quinoline", "91-63-4", "Khinaldin", "Chinaldine", "Quinoline, 2-methyl-", "NSC-3397", "DVG30M0M87"],
